__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
node_modules/
*.log
research/observer-*.json
var/
reasonix.toml
.reasonix/

# Scratch files the build and test targets create and normally clean up. An
# interrupted run leaves them behind, and neither is anything a reader wants.
.test.log
checker/dist/.build.js

# Go coverage and profile output, which `go test -coverprofile` writes wherever it
# is run from.
*.coverprofile
coverage.out
cover.out

# The built checker module. GENERATED from checker/src by
# `python3 tools/build_checker.py`, which `make check` runs in --check mode.
#
# Not committed: it is build output, and a generated file in a diff is noise a
# reviewer has to scroll past. `hedgecheck serve --checker checker/dist` needs it, so
# build once after a clone. The service says plainly when the module is absent rather
# than serving a page that silently offers no check.
checker/dist/

# NOT IGNORED, and deliberately so:
#   fixtures/** is generated and committed. It is the conformance corpus three
#   implementations are compared against, so it has to exist in a clone for
#   `make check` to mean anything, and each generator has a --check mode that fails
#   when the tree is stale.
